{
  "technical_and_design_decisions": [
    "All work targets the Spring Cloud Data Flow (admin server, StreamController, module/artifact registry) and Spring Cloud Stream codebases; Java 8+ with Maven multi-module builds and JUnit 4.",
    "U1/U2: Extract the Kafka and Rabbit JUnit @Rule test fixtures into two dedicated Git repositories (e.g., spring-cloud-stream-test-support-kafka and -rabbit), each with a standalone Maven build publishing versioned artifacts; existing projects switch from embedded copies to consuming the published artifacts.",
    "U3: Introduce a platform-neutral App Deployer SPI between the admin REST layer and runtime platforms; the admin REST API delegates to this SPI so behavior is identical across Cloud Foundry, YARN, and Lattice, each backed by a platform-specific deployer implementation.",
    "U4: Extend the artifact registry with a 'library' artifact type identified by Maven coordinates; include/exclude statements in stream definitions are resolved at definition/deployment time against registered libraries.",
    "U5: Support named channels via a DSL/parser extension that binds stream definitions directly to externally managed middleware destinations (topics/queues) without requiring source or sink modules; deployer binds named channels using standard binder destination properties.",
    "U6: StreamController API contracts verified with Spring MockMvc-based tests executed in the build (no live middleware required).",
    "U7: Stream name uniqueness enforced in the controller/service layer backed by the stream definition repository; violations return HTTP 409 Conflict with a clear error message.",
    "U8: Kinesis source implemented as a Spring Cloud Stream source module using the AWS Kinesis Client Library (KCL) with externalized configuration properties (stream name, region, credentials, checkpointing)."
  ],
  "assumptions": [
    "A single developer performs all work; estimates are pure effort (work-hours) excluding review queues, meetings, and wait time.",
    "Existing Spring Cloud Data Flow / Spring Cloud Stream codebases (admin server, StreamController, DSL parser, module registry) are available and buildable as the starting point.",
    "Test infrastructure is available: embedded Kafka/Rabbit or Docker-based brokers for U1/U2, LocalStack (or equivalent AWS mock) for Kinesis in U8, and accessible CF, YARN, and Lattice test environments for U3.",
    "New repositories for U1/U2 are created under the existing GitHub organization and reuse the established CI (Travis/Jenkins) and artifact publishing (snapshot/milestone) setup.",
    "Scope covers server-side code, DSL/parser, REST API, shell commands, and reference documentation; no web dashboard (UI) work is required.",
    "Backward compatibility must be preserved for existing stream definitions and REST clients.",
    "No formal performance/load testing or security audit is in scope beyond standard unit/integration tests."
  ],
  "activities": [
    {
      "activity_id": "A1",
      "activity_name": "Requirements analysis and increment planning",
      "activity_description": "Analyze the eight user stories, map them to affected components (test fixtures, admin server, deployer SPI, registry, DSL parser, StreamController, Kinesis module), define acceptance criteria, and sequence the work.",
      "most_likely_effort": 8
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A2",
      "activity_name": "Architecture and high-level design",
      "activity_description": "Design the App Deployer SPI abstraction (U3), the library registration and include/exclude resolution model (U4), the named-channel DSL extension (U5), and the extracted test-fixture artifact structure (U1/U2); produce design notes and interface sketches.",
      "most_likely_effort": 20
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A3",
      "activity_name": "U1: Extract Kafka @Rule to separate repository",
      "activity_description": "Create the new repository, move the Kafka JUnit rule and supporting classes, set up a standalone Maven build and artifact publishing, update spring-cloud-stream consumers to depend on the published artifact, adapt tests, and write README/docs.",
      "most_likely_effort": 20
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A4",
      "activity_name": "U2: Extract Rabbit @Rule to separate repository",
      "activity_description": "Repeat the extraction pattern for the Rabbit JUnit rule: new repository, standalone build and publishing, consumer migration to the external artifact, test adaptation, and documentation (benefits from U1 experience).",
      "most_likely_effort": 14
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A5",
      "activity_name": "U3: Consistent admin REST APIs across Lattice, YARN, and Cloud Foundry",
      "activity_description": "Define the platform-neutral App Deployer SPI, refactor the admin REST layer to delegate to it, implement/align the Cloud Foundry, YARN, and Lattice deployer implementations, normalize status/error mapping, and add per-platform integration tests proving consistent REST behavior.",
      "most_likely_effort": 110
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A6",
      "activity_name": "U4: Library artifact registration with include/exclude support",
      "activity_description": "Add a 'library' artifact type to the registry with Maven coordinate resolution, implement include/exclude resolution during stream definition parsing and deployment, add REST endpoints and shell commands for library registration, plus unit/integration tests and docs.",
      "most_likely_effort": 48
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A7",
      "activity_name": "U5: Named channels for pipelines without source/sink modules",
      "activity_description": "Extend the stream DSL/parser to reference externally managed destinations as named channels, implement binder binding/validation logic for named channels at deployment time, handle error cases (missing destination, conflicts), and add tests and reference documentation.",
      "most_likely_effort": 40
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A8",
      "activity_name": "U6: StreamController API contract test coverage",
      "activity_description": "Write comprehensive MockMvc-based tests for all StreamController endpoints (create, list, get, deploy, undeploy, destroy, validation errors), asserting HTTP status codes, payloads, and error contracts so they run at build time.",
      "most_likely_effort": 24
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A9",
      "activity_name": "U7: Enforce unique stream names",
      "activity_description": "Add duplicate-name validation in the controller/service layer backed by the stream definition repository, map violations to HTTP 409 with a clear message, and add unit and API tests covering create/rename edge cases.",
      "most_likely_effort": 10
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A10",
      "activity_name": "U8: Kinesis source module",
      "activity_description": "Implement the Kinesis source module using the AWS Kinesis Client Library (KCL): message consumption and mapping to Spring Messaging, externalized configuration properties (stream, region, credentials, checkpointing), binder integration, unit/integration tests against a LocalStack-style mock, and documentation.",
      "most_likely_effort": 48
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A11",
      "activity_name": "Cross-cutting integration and system testing",
      "activity_description": "End-to-end verification of the increment: build and deploy sample streams exercising named channels, library include/exclude, and the Kinesis source; verify admin REST consistency across the three platforms; regression-run the full build.",
      "most_likely_effort": 24
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A12",
      "activity_name": "Documentation and samples",
      "activity_description": "Update reference documentation and READMEs for the new test-fixture repositories, deployer SPI and platform notes, library registration, named channels, duplicate-name behavior, StreamController contracts, and the Kinesis source; add sample stream definitions.",
      "most_likely_effort": 16
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A13",
      "activity_name": "CI setup for new repositories and release preparation",
      "activity_description": "Configure CI pipelines and artifact publishing for the two new test-fixture repositories, wire new modules into the main build, perform version alignment, changelog, and release-candidate builds.",
      "most_likely_effort": 10
    }
  ],
  "reported_total": {
    "most_likely_effort": 392
  }
}
```

